\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The certificate in practice (\textsc  {Gas-Pce}). $\Delta (\hat  \eta _\mu )=4\hat  \eta _\mu /(1-\hat  \eta _\mu )$ is the guaranteed bound and ``measured'' is $\max _j|T_j(f^{\mathcal  {S}})-T_j(f^{\mathcal  {T}})|$, the quantity in the second half of Eq.~\ref {eq:cert}. The teacher's indices are themselves Monte-Carlo estimates, so the comparison cannot resolve below the reference estimator's own sampling error: ``floor'' is that error, measured by estimating the teacher's indices twice from independent samples, and ``holds'' tests measured $\le \Delta +$floor. Where floor~$>\Delta $ the experiment is limited by the reference, not by the bound.}}{8}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:certificate}{{3}{8}{The certificate in practice (\GASPCE ). $\Delta (\hat \eta _\mu )=4\hat \eta _\mu /(1-\hat \eta _\mu )$ is the guaranteed bound and ``measured'' is $\max _j|T_j(\fS )-T_j(\fT )|$, the quantity in the second half of Eq.~\ref {eq:cert}. The teacher's indices are themselves Monte-Carlo estimates, so the comparison cannot resolve below the reference estimator's own sampling error: ``floor'' is that error, measured by estimating the teacher's indices twice from independent samples, and ``holds'' tests measured $\le \Delta +$floor. Where floor~$>\Delta $ the experiment is limited by the reference, not by the bound}{table.3}{}}
\newlabel{tab:paired}{{5}{8}{(a) Fidelity, and who wins}{section*.17}{}}
